VAXION512 - ARCHITECTURAL DESIGN SPECIFICATION (MATHEMATICAL EDITION)\
Version: 1.1.0\
Target Architecture: Intel x86_64 (AVX-512F, AVX-512DQ)\
Classification: Technical / Mathematical Documentation\
Status: Final Release\
\
\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
MATHEMATICAL MODEL\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 The algorithm executes a vector transformation V_in -> V_out leveraging 512-bit parallelism. Let M be an input vector consisting of eight 64-bit words:\
M = [m_0, m_1, ..., m_7], where m_i is an element of \{0, 1\}^64\
Each batch processes four such vectors (M_0, M_1, M_2, M_3). The transformation equation for a single vector is defined as:\
V_out = ((V_in XOR R_mask) >>> Delta_p) XOR K_anchor\
Where:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
XOR represents the exclusive OR bitwise operation.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
represents the Circular Right Rotation.\uc0\u8232 \u8232 \
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
R_mask is the correction mask retrieved from the LUT (broadcasted to 512-bit width).\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Delta_p is the rotation magnitude.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
K_anchor is the fixed 512-bit anchor vector.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
TECHNICAL IMPLEMENTATION AND EQUATION MAPPING\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 2.1. Bit-Level Parallelism (Data Expansion)\
When a value 'r' is retrieved from the LUT (R_mask), it is expanded (broadcasted) into a vector:\
vec(R) = [r, r, r, r, r, r, r, r]\
This enables SIMD (Single Instruction, Multiple Data) operations, where eight words are transformed simultaneously.\
2.2. The Rotation Engine (Circular Shift)\
In standard algebra, a right shift (>>) discards bits. VAxion512 utilizes the 'vprorvq' instruction, which implements mathematical rotation:\
(x >>> n) = (x >> n) OR (x << (64 - n))\
This preserves the entropy of the data, which is critical for the algorithm's determinism.\
\
\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
ASSEMBLY OPERATION CYCLE ANALYSIS\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Operations are chained to ensure the Intel instruction pipeline remains saturated without stalls.\
\
Phase | Intel Instruction | Mathematical Operation | Explanation\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Load | vmovdqa64 | Z_k <- K_anchor | Load anchor from cache.\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
XOR I | vpxorq | Z_0 <- M_in XOR vec(R) | Primary mixing phase.\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Rotate | vprorvq | Z_0 <- Z_0 >>> vec(Delta) | Vectorized rotation (8 words).\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
XOR II | vpxorq | Z_0 <- Z_0 XOR Z_k | Final anchoring phase.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
