\ls6\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
ERROR DETECTION (PARITY FUNCTION)\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Finally, the algorithm calculates a parity mask P_mask according to the following logic:\
P_mask = Sum from j=0 to 3 of ( [V_out,j != 0] * 2^j )\
In practice, if a single bit in the vector V_out is set to 1, the corresponding bit in the mask register activates. This is implemented via the 'vptestmq' instruction, which is mathematically:\
k_res = NOT (Z_out AND Z_out == 0)\
\
