\ls7\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
THEORETICAL PERFORMANCE PEAK\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 On Intel processors equipped with dual 512-bit FMA units (e.g., Xeon Ice Lake), the theoretical throughput (T_max) is:\
T_max = 2 instructions/cycle * 64 bytes/instruction * f (Hz)\
At a 3.0 GHz clock frequency, this results in:\
T_max = 2 * 64 * 3.0 * 10^9 approx. 384 GB/s (from L1 Cache)\
\
